  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14162998/assets/9c14d7a4f9a460c3219cb457ff9f8ba8fb32a22101dfba3e0925aa8077b011cf.png)\n\nIn the figure above, $∠ABC$ is an angle and $D$ is a point in the interior of $∠ABC$ such that $m∠CBD=5x+{3}^{∘}.$ If $m∠ABC={106}^{∘}$ and $∠CBD≅∠ABD$, find the value of $x.$",
  "worked_solution": "By the angle addition postulate,\n\n$$\nm∠ABC=m∠ABD+m∠CBD.\n$$\n\nSince $∠CBD≅∠ABD$, then we have $m∠CBD=m∠ABD.$  Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠ABC & =m∠ABD+m∠CBD \\\\  & =m∠CBD+m∠CBD \\\\  & =2m∠CBD.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the fact that $m∠CBD=5x+{3}^{∘}$ and $m∠ABC={106}^{∘},$ we can solve for $x$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{106}^{∘} & =2(5x+3) \\\\ {106}^{∘} & =10x+{6}^{∘} \\\\ {100}^{∘} & =10x \\\\ {10}^{∘} & =x \\\\ x & ={10}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
